a crt filter for the nes and snes

0027 hid the shader row for both consoles, because every shader slot had
imitated an LCD and a television never had one. Played on a 3.5" panel at
2x or 2.5x, the picture looks like a scaled-up bitmap instead. This adds
one filter that suits a television, CRT, and makes it the default for the
NES and the SNES. This is a UX change on purpose, and it touches slot-ui
for the same reason 0027 did.

The filter. Each source row gets a dark band across its lower half, the
gap between scanlines, at 60% brightness, and an aperture grille gives
every panel column one phosphor at full strength and the other two at
85%. A 1.2 gain pays back most of what those take away, and saturates on
white rather than dimming it. At 2x every second panel row is a gap. At
2.5x (the picture stretched to the panel's height) source rows land on
2, 3, 2, 3 panel rows. Sampling the band at a row's centre would give
some source rows no dark line at all, so the band is averaged over each
panel row's extent, and every source row keeps one.

The cost. Like Lcd3x, the mask is separable: the gap depends only on the
row and the grille only on the column. So it goes into the game pass's
existing tables. The grille is the column table's factors, at most 1.0,
which keeps s * k inside a u16. The gap and the gain are the row factor,
whose kernel already saturates. The inner loop and the NEON kernel do not
change, so CRT costs the same per pixel as Off: one table rebuild when
the picture moves, and one crt_row() per panel row.

Settings. shader_nes and shader_snes are kept in slot.state and offer Off
and CRT (`Shader::TV`). A card that names an LCD shader for either falls
back to CRT. In game, the Shader row comes back for both consoles and
steps that console alone, and so does the shader shortcut, with a
"Shader: CRT" toast. Colour correction stays hidden.

The GL path has the same mask as a `u_mode > 4.5` branch of GAME_FRAG,
for the desktop build.

Tested: crt_tests compares the software pass against crt_row and
crt_column evaluated in floats per pixel, at 2x and stretched (worst
difference 2), and checks that a dark line survives 2.5x. in_game_menu
steps the NES row and checks that the SNES keeps its own value.
durability round-trips the new keys and rejects lcd3x on a console. The
failures in app, e2e, eject, layout, play and render_link_screen are the
same set on the tree before this patch. Not yet run on the handheld.

Applies on top of 0042, upstream 91499a9.

